======================== DATASET VALUE ==============================
1-10  --  Audio with text
11-20 --  Audio only

======================== DATASET RULES ==============================
1. Numbers
--- Change: ('3' -> 'trei')
--- Always use written form, never digits

2. Repeated words — match what you hear exactly
--- Hesitation/false start with pause  →  'mai... mai mult'
--- Emphatic repetition with beat      →  'mai, mai mult'
--- Fluid rhythmic repetition          →  'mai mai mult'
--- Never collapse any of these to 'mai mult' — speaker said it

3. Incomplete words
--- Change: ('deas... deasupra' -> 'deasupra')
--- Fragments have no value and break tokenizers

4. Correct word mappings
    a. Phonetic reductions
    --- Change: ('iestea' -> 'acestea')
    --- Change: ('sâ meargă' -> 'să meargă')
    --- Change: ('sâ duce' -> 'se duce')
    --- Flag ambiguous cases for review

    b. Lexical regionalisms — normalize to standard Romanian
    --- Change: ('mâca' -> 'bunica')
    --- Only apply when a clear standard Romanian equivalent exists
    --- If no clean equivalent exists -> mark with '2' for review

5. Grammatical errors — keep as said
--- Keep: ('Deja a doilea oară')
--- <???> Keep: ('s-o dus') and do not force into ('s-a dus') or ('s-au dus')
--- <???> Write exactly what you hear every time - Given that the word is correct

6. Punctuation - For now no real rules

7. Capitalization
--- Capitalize sentence starts and proper nouns only
--- ('moldova' -> 'Moldova', 'chișinău' -> 'Chișinău')

8. Foreign / Russian words
--- English: keep as spoken, including inflected forms
    - influencer/influencerii/influencer-ul
    - Vocalic suffixes: no hyphen ('influencerii', 'influenceri')
    - Consonantal suffixes: use hyphen ('influencer-ul', 'blogger-ul')
    - Follow standard Romanian orthography for loanword inflection
--- Russian: change common used words in Moldova with alternatives in romanian
    - Change: ('davai' -> 'hai')
    - Mark with '2' for later review
--- Other Languages: I avoid other languages.

9. Inaudible or unclear audio
--- Never guess, never leave blank  -  Mark Segment with '0', as BAD.


======================== DATASET LOGIC ==============================
"id"    - audio segment identification
"start" - start time of audio segment
"end"   - end time of audio segment
"text"  - The actual sentence the User says
    --- Contains dublicates like "pe cer mai... mai sus"
    --- Not normalised: "să-mi dea" not normalised in "să îmi dea"
    --- Some words normalised(consult changed_words.json)
"id_user" - ID of user that speaks
    --- Each Video starts from id_user 1, so all videos will have ID 1, but different speakers
    --- ID 7 is for THE hosts in the show, so there are multiple persons under ID 7 of the same VIDEO
"info" - Has values that characterise only the TEXT quality
    --- can have only 0 or 1 or 2 like: 0..., 1..., 2..., + in combination with others [3-9]
    --- 0 - BAD, DO NOT USE FOR DATASET
    --- 1 - Perfect
    --- 2 - Needs corrections maybe, but still usable
    --- 9 - Signifies Background NOISE(may affect voice). Placed after 0,1,2. (ex: "09", "19")


======================== Set Up =====================================
sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3-tk ffmpeg python3-venv python3-pip
python3 -m venv v_environment
source v_environment/bin/activate

pip install -r requirements.txt
pip install -r req_just_edit.txt

